H300.definition:
from H251 (אָח) and H7837 (שַׁחַר); brother of (the) dawn;
Achishachar, an Israelite
KJV: Ahishar.

H301.definition:
from H251 (אָח) and H7891 (שִׁיר); brother of (the) singer;
Achishar, an Israelite
KJV: Ahishar.

H302.definition:
from H251 (אָח) and H8602 (תָּפֵל); brother of folly;
Achithophel, an Israelite
KJV: Ahithophel.

H303.definition:
from the same root as H2459 (חֶלֶב); fatness (i.e. fertile);
Achlab, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ahlab.

H304.definition:
the same as H305 (אַחֲלַי); wishful;
Achlai, the name of an Israelitess and of an Israelite
KJV: Ahlai.

H305.definition:
or אַחֲלֵי; prob from H253 (אָח) and a variation of H3863 (לוּא);
would that!
KJV: O that, would God.

H306.definition:
perhaps from H2492 (חָלַם) (and thus dream-stone);
a gem, probably the amethyst
KJV: amethyst.

H307.definition:
of Persian derivation;
Achmetha (i.e. Ecbatana), the summer capital of Persia
KJV: Achmetha.

H308.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Achasbai, an Israelite
KJV: Ahasbai.

H309.definition:
a primitive root;
to loiter (i.e. be behind); by implication to procrastinate
KJV: continue, defer, delay, hinder, be late (slack), stay (there), tarry (longer).

H310.definition:
from H309 (אָחַר);
properly, the hind part; generally used as an adverb or conjunction, after (in various senses)
KJV: after (that, -ward), again, at, away from, back (from, -side), behind, beside, by, follow (after, -ing), forasmuch, from, hereafter, hinder end, [phrase] out (over) live, [phrase] persecute, posterity, pursuing, remnant, seeing, since, thence(-forth), when, with.

H311.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H310 (אַחַר);
after
KJV: (here-) after.

H312.definition:
from H309 (אָחַר);
properly, hinder; generally, next, other, etc.
KJV: (an-) other man, following, next, strange.

H313.definition:
the same as H312 (אַחֵר);
Acher, an Israelite
KJV: Aher.

H314.definition:
or (shortened) אַחֲרֹן; from H309 (אָחַר);
hinder; generally, late or last; specifically (as facing the east) western
KJV: after (-ward), to come, following, hind(-er, -ermost, -most), last, latter, rereward, ut(ter) most.

H315.definition:
from H310 (אַחַר) and H251 (אָח); after (his) brother;
Achrach, an Israelite
KJV: Aharah.

H316.definition:
from H310 (אַחַר) and H2426 (חֵיל); behind (the) intrenchment (i.e. safe);
Acharchel, an Israelite
KJV: Aharhel,

H318.definition:
(Aramaic) or (shortened) אׇחֳרֵן; (Aramaic) from H317 (אׇחֳרִי);
last
KJV: at last.

H319.definition:
from H310 (אַחַר);
the last or end, hence, the future; also posterity
KJV: (last, latter) end (time), hinder (utter) -most, length, posterity, remnant, residue, reward.

H320.definition:
(Aramaic) from H311 (אַחַר); the same as H319 (אַחֲרִית);
later
KJV: latter.

H321.definition:
(Aramaic) from H311 (אַחַר); the same as H317 (אׇחֳרִי);
other
KJV: (an-) other.

H322.definition:
prolonged from H268 (אָחוֹר);
backwards
KJV: back (-ward, again).

H323.definition:
of Persian derivation;
a satrap or governorof amain province (of Persia)
KJV: lieutenant.

H324.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H323 (אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפַּן)
{a satrap or governorof amain province (of Persia)}
KJV: prince.

H325.definition:
or (shortened) אַחַשְׁרֹשׁ (Esther 10:1); of Persian origin;
Achashverosh (i.e. Ahasuerus or Artaxerxes, but in this case Xerxes), the title (rather than name) of a Persian king
KJV: Ahasuerus.

H326.definition:
probably of Persian derivation;
an achastarite (i.e. courier); the designation (rather than name) of an Israelite
KJV: Haakashtari (includ. the article).

H327.definition:
of Persian origin;
a mule
KJV: camel.

H328.definition:
from an unused root perhaps meaning to move softly;
(as a noun) a necromancer (from their soft incantations), (as an adverb) gently
KJV: charmer, gently, secret, softly.

H329.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to pierce or make fast;
a thorn-tree (especially the buckthorn)
KJV: Atad, bramble, thorn.

H330.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to bind);
properly, twisted (yarn), i.e. tapestry
KJV: fine linen.

H331.definition:
a primitive root;
to close (the lips or ears); by analology to contract (a window by bevelled jambs)
KJV: narrow, shut, stop.

H332.definition:
a primitive root;
to close up
KJV: shut.

H333.definition:
from H332 (אָטַר); maimed;
Ater, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Ater.

H334.definition:
from H332 (אָטַר);
shut up, i.e. impeded (as to the use of the right hand)
KJV: [phrase] left-handed.

H335.definition:
perhaps from H370 (אַיִן);
where? hence how?
KJV: how, what, whence, where, whether, which (way).

H336.definition:
probably identical with H335 (אַי) (through the idea of a query);
not
KJV: island (Job 22:30).

H337.definition:
short from H188 (אוֹי);
alas!
KJV: woe.

H338.definition:
probably identical with H337 (אִי) (through the idea of a doleful sound);
a howler (used only in the plural), i.e. any solitary wild creature
KJV: wild beast of the islands.

H339.definition:
from H183 (אָוָה);
properly, a habitable spot (as desirable); dry land, a coast, an island
KJV: country, isle, island.

H340.definition:
a primitive root;
to hate (as one of an opposite tribe or party); hence to be hostile
KJV: be an enemy.

H341.definition:
or (fully) אוֹיֵב; active participle of H340 (אָיַב);
hating; an adversary
KJV: enemy, foe.

H342.definition:
from H340 (אָיַב);
hostility
KJV: emnity, hatred.

H343.definition:
from the same as H181 (אוּד) (in the sense of bending down);
oppression; by implication misfortune, ruin
KJV: calamity, destruction.

H344.definition:
perhaps from H337 (אִי);
the screamer, i.e. a hawk
KJV: kite, vulture.

H345.definition:
the same as H344 (אַיָּה);
Ajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Aiah, Ajah.

H346.definition:
prolonged from H335 (אַי);
where?
KJV: where.

H347.definition:
from H340 (אָיַב); hated (i.e. persecuted);
Ijob, the patriarch famous for his patience
KJV: Job.

H348.definition:
from H336 (אִי)lemma אי missing vowel, corrected to אִי and H2083 (זְבֻל);
Izebel, the wife of king Ahab
KJV: Jezebel.

H349.definition:
also אֵיכָה ; and אֵיכָכָה ; prolonged from H335 (אַי);
how? or how!; also where
KJV: how, what.

H350.definition:
from H336 (אִי)lemma אי missing vowel, corrected to אִי and H3519 (כָּבוֹד); (there is) no glory, i.e. inglorious;
Ikabod, a son of Phineas
KJV: I-chabod.

H351.definition:
probably a variation for H349 (אֵיךְ), but not as an interogative;
where
KJV: where.

H352.definition:
from the same as H193 (אוּל);
properly, strength; hence, anything strong; specifically a chief (politically); also a ram (from his strength); a pilaster (as a strong support); an oak or other strong tree
KJV: mighty (man), lintel, oak, post, ram, tree.

H353.definition:
a variation of H352 (אַיִל);
strength
KJV: strength.

H354.definition:
an intensive form of H352 (אַיִל) (in the sense of ram);
a stag or male deer
KJV: hart.

H355.definition:
feminine of H354 (אַיָּל);
a doe or female deer
KJV: hind.

H356.definition:
or (shortened) אֵלוֹן ; or אֵילֹן ; from H352 (אַיִל); oak-grove;
Elon, the name of a place in Palestine, and also of one Hittite, two Israelites
KJV: Elon.

H357.definition:
from H354 (אַיָּל); deer-field;
Ajalon, the name of five places in Palestine
KJV: Aijalon, Ajalon.

H358.definition:
from H356 (אֵילוֹן), H1004 (בַּיִת), and H2603 (חָנַן); oak-grove of (the) house of favor;
Elon of Beth-chanan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Elon-bethhanan.

H359.definition:
or אֵילַת ; from H352 (אַיִל); trees or a grove (i.e. palms);
Eloth or Elath, a place on the Red Sea
KJV: Elath, Eloth.

H360.definition:
feminine of H353 (אֱיָל);
power; by implication, protection
KJV: strength.

H361.definition:
or (shortened) אֵלָם ; or (feminine) אֵלַמָּה ; probably from H352 (אַיִל);
a pillar-space (or colonnade), i.e. a pale (or portico)
KJV: arch.

H362.definition:
plural of H352 (אַיִל); palm-trees;
Elim, a place in the Desert
KJV: Elim.

H363.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H356 (אֵילוֹן);
a tree
KJV: tree.

H364.definition:
from H352 (אַיִל) and H6290 (פָּארָן); oak of Paran;
El-Paran, a portion of the district of Paran
KJV: El-paran.

H365.definition:
the same as H355 (אַיָּלָה);
a doe
KJV: hind, Aijeleth.

H366.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to frighten);
frightful
KJV: terrible.

H367.definition:
or (shortened) אֵמָה; from the same as H366 (אָיֹם);
fright; concrete, an idol (as a bugbear)
KJV: dread, fear, horror, idol, terrible, terror.

H368.definition:
plural of H367 (אֵימָה); terrors;
Emim, an early Canaanitish (or Maobitish) tribe
KJV: Emims.

H369.definition:
as if from a primitive root meaning to be nothing or not exist;
a non-entity; generally used as a negative particle
KJV: else, except, fail, (father-) less, be gone, in(-curable), neither, never, no (where), none, nor, (any, thing), not, nothing, to nought, past, un(-searchable), well-nigh, without. Compare H370 (אַיִן).

H371.definition:
apparently a shortened form of H369 (אַיִן); but (like H370 (אַיִן)) an interrogative;
is it not?
KJV: not.

H372.definition:
from H336 (אִי)lemma אי missing vowel, corrected to אִי and H5828 (עֵזֶר); helpless;
Iezer, an Israelite
KJV: Jeezer.

H373.definition:
patronymic from H372 (אִיעֶזֵר);
an Iezrite or descendant of Iezer
KJV: Jezerite.

H374.definition:
or (shortened) אֵפָה ; of Egyptian derivation;
an ephah or measure for grain; hence, a measure in general
KJV: ephah, (divers) measure(-s).

H375.definition:
from H335 (אַי) and H6311 (פֹּה);
what place?; also (of time) when?; or (of means) how?
KJV: what manner, where.

H376.definition:
contracted for H582 (אֱנוֹשׁ) (or perhaps rather from an unused root meaning to be extant);
a man as an individual or a male person; often used as an adjunct to a more definite term (and in such cases frequently not expressed in translation)
KJV: also, another, any (man), a certain, [phrase] champion, consent, each, every (one), fellow, (foot-, husband-) man, (good-, great, mighty) man, he, high (degree), him (that is), husband, man(-kind), [phrase] none, one, people, person, [phrase] steward, what (man) soever, whoso(-ever), worthy. Compare H802 (אִשָּׁה).

H377.definition:
denominative from H376 (אִישׁ);
to be a man, i.e. act in amanly way
KJV: show (one) self a man.

H378.definition:
from H376 (אִישׁ) and H1322 (בֹּשֶׁת); man of shame;
Ish-Bosheth, a son of King Saul
KJV: Ish-bosheth.

H379.definition:
from H376 (אִישׁ) and H1935 (הוֹד); man of renown;
Ishod, an Israelite
KJV: Ishod.

H380.definition:
diminutive from H376 (אִישׁ);
the little man of the eye; the pupil or ball; hence, the middle (of night)
KJV: apple (of the eye), black, obscure.

H381.definition:
from H376 (אִישׁ) and H2428 (חַיִל); man of might; by defective transcription (2 Samuel 23:20) אִישׁ־חַיxlit ʼÎsh-Chay corrected to ʼÎysh-Chay; as if from H376 (אִישׁ) and H2416 (חַי); living man;
Ishchail (or Ish-chai), an Israelite
KJV: a valiant man.

H382.definition:
from H376 (אִישׁ) and H2897 (טוֹב); man of Tob;
Ish-Tob, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ish-tob.

H383.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3426 (יֵשׁ);
properly, entity; used only as aparticle of affirmation, there is
KJV: art thou, can, do ye, have, it be, there is (are), [idiom] we will not.

H384.definition:
perhaps from H837 (אֹשֶׁר) and H410 (אֵל); God has arrived;
Ithiel, the name of an Israelite, also of a symbolical person
KJV: Ithiel.

H385.definition:
from H339 (אִי) and H8558 (תָּמָר); coast of the palm-tree;
Ithamar, a son of Aaron
KJV: Ithamar.

H386.definition:
or (shortened) אֵתָן ; from an unused root (meaning to continue);
permanence; hence (concrete) permanent; specifically a chieftain
KJV: hard, mighty, rough, strength, strong.

H387.definition:
the same as H386 (אֵיתָן); permanent;
Ethan, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Ethan.

H388.definition:
plural of H386 (אֵיתָן); always with the article; the permanent brooks;
Ethanim, the name of a month
KJV: Ethanim.

H389.definition:
akin to H403 (אָכֵן);
a particle of affirmation, surely; hence (by limitation) only
KJV: also, in any wise, at least, but, certainly, even, howbeit, nevertheless, notwithstanding, only, save, surely, of a surety, truly, verily, [phrase] wherefore, yet (but).

H390.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to strengthen; a fortress;
Accad, a place in Babylon
KJV: Accad.

H391.definition:
from H3576 (כָּזַב);
falsehood; by implication treachery
KJV: liar, lie.

H392.definition:
from H391 (אַכְזָב); deceitful (in the sense of a winter-torrent which fails in summer);
Akzib, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Achzib.

H393.definition:
from an unused root (apparently meaning to act harshly);
violent; by implication deadly; also (in a good sense) brave
KJV: cruel, fierce.

H396.definition:
feminine from H398 (אָכַל);
something eatable, i.e. food
KJV: meat.

H397.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Akish, a Philistine king
KJV: Achish.

H398.definition:
a primitive root;
to eat (literally or figuratively)
KJV: [idiom] at all, burn up, consume, devour(-er, up), dine, eat(-er, up), feed (with), food, [idiom] freely, [idiom] in...wise(-deed, plenty), (lay) meat, [idiom] quite.

H399.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H398 (אָכַל)
{to eat (literally or figuratively)}
KJV: [phrase] accuse, devour, eat.
